.TH "SOPLOS-THEME-MANAGER" "1" "2026-11-16" "Soplos Linux" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
soplos-theme-manager \- theme manager for Soplos Linux Tyron (Xfce)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B soplos-theme-manager
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIFILE.sth\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B soplos-theme-manager
manages the look of Soplos Linux Tyron from a graphical interface. Built with
Tauri 2, Rust, and Svelte, it has eight pages:
.IP \[bu] 2
.B Themes:
the complete desktop themes (GTK theme, icons, cursor, fonts, window borders,
wallpaper and panel) that were saved. A theme can be applied, deleted, exported
to a
.B .sth
file and imported from one. Six themes come with the program and are added the
first time it runs.
.IP \[bu]
.B Wallpapers:
the pictures of a folder and of the folders inside it. A picture is set as the
wallpaper of every screen and workspace, and new pictures can be installed for
one user or for every user.
.IP \[bu]
.B GTK Themes, Icons
and
.B Cursors:
the installed themes of each kind, as cards. A GTK theme is drawn with its own
colors, an icon theme with some of its icons and a cursor theme with some of its
cursors. A click on a card applies the theme. Themes are installed from a package
(.tar.gz, .tar.xz, .tar.bz2, .tar or .zip) and deleted after a confirmation; the
active theme is never deleted.
.IP \[bu]
.B Panel:
the panels of Xfce, with their position, appearance, behavior and plugins.
The changes of every panel are applied together, and the panel is restarted once.
.IP \[bu]
.B Dock:
the applications pinned to the Docklike Taskbar, edited by dragging them on the
preview of the dock.
.IP \[bu]
.B Login Screen:
the settings of the LightDM GTK greeter: the background, the user picture, the
GTK, icon and cursor themes, the font and the position of the login box.
.P
The window never runs as root. The changes that need the administrator (the login
screen, and the themes and wallpapers installed for every user) go through a
single Polkit-gated helper, authenticated with
.BR pkexec (1),
which accepts only a closed list of operations and checks every value before it
writes.
.P
The settings of Xfce are read and written through
.BR xfconf-query (1).
A theme that carries a panel restarts the panel with
.BR xfce4-panel (1).
.P
The interface is available in English, Spanish, German, French, Italian,
Portuguese, Romanian and Russian. It starts in the system language and falls
back to English. The light or dark theme of the window follows the one of Xfce.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show summary of options.
.TP
.I FILE.sth
Open the theme in
.I FILE
and offer to install it. A double click on a
.B .sth
file in the file manager does the same.
.TP
.B \-\-run-ops \fIFILE\fR
Internal Polkit-authenticated task: validate and run the operations stored in
.IR FILE .
Used by the application itself through
.BR pkexec (1)
and not meant to be called by hand.
.SH KEYBOARD SHORTCUTS
.TP
.B F1
About dialog.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Q
Quit the application.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Tab
Next page.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+Tab
Previous page.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/soplos-theme-manager/themes/
The saved themes.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/soplos-theme-manager/thumbs/
Small copies of the wallpapers, made once so the pages show quickly.
.TP
.I /usr/share/soplos-theme-manager/base-themes/
The themes that come with the program.
.TP
.I /usr/share/themes/, ~/.themes/
Installed GTK themes.
.TP
.I /usr/share/icons/, ~/.icons/
Installed icon and cursor themes.
.TP
.I /usr/share/backgrounds/, ~/.local/share/backgrounds/
Wallpapers.
.TP
.I /etc/lightdm/lightdm-gtk-greeter.conf
The settings of the login screen.
.TP
.I /usr/share/polkit-1/actions/org.soplos.thememanager.policy
Polkit policy defining the administrator privileges for the installation for every user and for the login screen.
